A||||12||FieroKyle||2 Deer accidents this week!||||8||
Z||000000||FieroKyle||12-04-2001||12:44 AM||||Wednesday night coming home from work. Hit a deer, not too much damage, car very driveable.<P>Saturday night, coming from a party to go rent a movie (I was not in drunk whatsoever), wham hit a deer get stuck im the ditch. This guy in the Jeep pulls me out. This was all with my Regal beater. The second dear I hit a 1/4 mile from Fierowrecker's house, probably can see the tracks in the ditch where my car went in. I end of putting the deer in my trunk and took it back to the party. This guy helped me gutted it (ok pretty much he did gut it, I didn't feel like gutting a deer whatsoever that night, I have gutting one once). So now the deer is hanging my friend's garage.<P>The Buick is tore up pretty bad. Fascia, headlight moldings, and left fender is dusted. If anyone knows where or has parts, I would like them. 85' Buick Regal.<P>The headlights is held together with wire. It sucks big time. The car is pretty much not driveable at night past 10 miles. This just pisses me of royal. This is gonna delay many things I had planned for the Fiero (rims, lowering, new exhaust) I thought about bring the Fiero outta storage but figured I should use that $125 payment towards parts. Its really nice weather here and hasn't snowed so it was an option. Anyways thats it. ||||reg||8
Z||000001||AusFiero||12-04-2001||02:54 AM||||hmm they wasn't reindeer was they? If so should I expect Santa to be a bit late this year  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero3.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||12-04-2001||03:37 AM||||First thing you should do if you see a deer is get on the horn.  It'll usually startle them so they run off the road instead of standing there waiting to get hit.  I got to experiance first hand how this worked last week.. Deer was sitting on the right side of the road, staring into my headlights.  Lay on the horn and it immediatly darts off into the woods.<P>At least you didn't smack 'em with your Fiero...<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroBUZZ||12-04-2001||10:54 AM||||My son swerved to avoid one yesterday (I always told him to hit 'em) and rolled our van (Ford Rollostar).  No injuries to anyone. And no charges.<P>THE MORAL&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; hit a deer =comprehensive insurance not at fault.<BR>avoid deer and crash =collision insurance you are at fault.  No dead deer is no proof of actual deer on the road..cop didn't believe one of the 8 deer in the field may have been the culprit.<BR>FOLKS...HIT THE DAMN CRITTERS!!!!!SAVE $<BR>Gary||||reg||1
